{
  "cells": [
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Lecture 27 — Backpropagation: Sending the Error Backward\n","\n","Read the story first: [`blog.md`](<blog.md>). This lab reconstructs the same scalar network and numbers.\n"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Step 1 — Problem\n","\n","A first-layer weight does not touch the final loss directly. How can we calculate its effect without expanding the whole network?"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Step 2 — Prediction\n","\n","For $x=2,w=3,v=4,y=30$, predict $z$, $\\hat y$, $L$, and $dL/dw$ before running code."]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["x = 2.0\n","w = 3.0\n","v = 4.0\n","y = 30.0\n","\n","z = w * x\n","y_hat = v * z\n","loss = (y_hat - y) ** 2\n","\n","print(z, y_hat, loss)\n","assert z == 6.0\n","assert y_hat == 24.0\n","assert loss == 36.0\n"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Step 4 — Mathematics\n","\n","The chain rule is $dL/dw=(dL/d\\hat y)(d\\hat y/dz)(dz/dw)$.\n"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["dL_dyhat = 2 * (y_hat - y)\n","dyhat_dz = v\n","dz_dw = x\n","dL_dw = dL_dyhat * dyhat_dz * dz_dw\n","\n","assert dL_dyhat == -12.0\n","assert dyhat_dz == 4.0\n","assert dz_dw == 2.0\n","assert dL_dw == -96.0\n","print('dL/dw =', dL_dw)\n"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Step 6 — first implementation: explicit backward pass\n","upstream = 1.0\n","local_loss = 2 * (y_hat - y)\n","grad_z = upstream * local_loss * v\n","grad_w = grad_z * x\n","\n","assert grad_z == -48.0\n","assert grad_w == -96.0\n","print('grad_z:', grad_z, 'grad_w:', grad_w)\n"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["# Step 7 — visualization: loss as w changes\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import numpy as np\n","\n","ws = np.linspace(0, 5, 101)\n","losses = [(v * (ww * x) - y) ** 2 for ww in ws]\n","\n","plt.figure()\n","plt.plot(ws, losses)\n","plt.xlabel('w')\n","plt.ylabel('loss')\n","plt.title('Loss as the first weight changes')\n","plt.show()\n"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["# Step 8 — controlled experiment\n","# Change only w.\n","for ww in [2.5, 3.0, 3.5]:\n","    yhat = v * (ww * x)\n","    l = (yhat - y) ** 2\n","    g = 2 * (yhat - y) * v * x\n","    print(f'w={ww}: loss={l:.1f}, gradient={g:.1f}')\n"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["# Step 9 — numerical finite difference check\n","h = 1e-6\n","def f(ww):\n","    return (v * (ww * x) - y) ** 2\n","\n","finite_difference = (f(w + h) - f(w - h)) / (2 * h)\n","assert np.isclose(finite_difference, dL_dw, atol=1e-6)\n","print('finite difference:', finite_difference)\n"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Step 10 — Observe\n","\n","The finite-difference estimate agrees with the chain-rule gradient, and the loss changes as predicted when only $w$ moves."]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Step 11 — Explain\n","\n","Each local derivative answers one small question. Multiplying them carries sensitivity backward through the chain."]},
    {"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["# Step 12 — challenge\n","# YOUR CODE HERE\n","# 1. Derive dL/dv by the same method.\n","# 2. Add a third scalar operation and propagate its gradient.\n","# 3. Create a branching computation and add gradient contributions at the merge.\n"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Step 13 — Reflection\n","\n","Mastery checklist: explain the forward graph; write each local derivative; multiply along a path; add when paths merge; and distinguish backpropagation from the optimizer.\n","\n","**Next:** pack the same scalar reasoning into matrix formulas for $dW$, $db$, and $dX$.\"]}
